  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "When a scale constraint is attached to a bone in an avatar, and you scale the avatar in-game, the scale factor is applied double to the bone in question. That is, if I set a scale constraint pointing to a transform whose scale is always 1,1,1, then doubling the scale of my avatar will quadruple the world scale of the target of the scale constraint.\n\nThis effect occurs only in client; scaling the root of the avatar in the unity editor does not have this effect, so something strange seems to be happening in the VRChat client here.\n\nI've uploaded an avatar which reproduces this issue here: avtr_4fea6b0c-ed50-467c-97d1-bdfa7ec03169\n\nThe expected behavior is that both spheres should have the same size; one has no constraints on it, the other is linked by a scale constraint to an object under the avatar root which always has 0.1 scale.\n\nThis bug impacts the popular \"marshmallow PB\" booth asset, resulting in what could perhaps be charitably referred to as \"breast explosions\".",
